# PAUSED -- the automated run is switched off for now.
#
# The schedule below is left here commented out so it can be turned back on
# without rewriting it. Two things have to happen for an automated run to send:
#
#   1. Uncomment the line below and install it with: crontab -e
#   2. Set AUTOMATION_ENABLED=1 in .env
#
# Without step 2 the job still fires and the run exits with a "paused" log
# line, having scraped nothing and sent nothing.
#
# While paused, reminders go out from the dashboard: click Sync portal, review
# who is eligible, then send.

# Run the assessment reminder every weekday at 9:00 AM ET (13:00 UTC)
# Logs go to assessment-reminder/logs/reminder.log
#
# manage.py at the repository root dispatches to backend/mail/reminder.py, and
# every path the run needs is resolved from the repository root rather than from
# cwd -- which is why the `cd` below matters and the rest does not.
#
# THE COMMAND CHANGED ONCE. It used to be `python3 reminder.py`, back when there
# was a launcher file per command. If you are looking at an installed crontab
# that still says that, it is stale and the run is failing silently into
# logs/cron.log -- replace the line with this one.

# 0 13 * * 1-5 cd /opt/assessment-reminder && /usr/bin/env python3 manage.py reminder >> logs/cron.log 2>&1
